Third-party binaries redistributed in bin/:

All binaries are armv7 (32-bit ARM) builds.  SHA-256 checksums are in
bin/SHA256SUMS.  Full license texts are in LICENSES/.

  * mirakc
    https://github.com/mirakc/mirakc -- MIT OR Apache-2.0
    (LICENSES/MIT-mirakc.txt, LICENSE)
    Built from the fork https://github.com/mikuta0407/mirakc, branch
    feat/for-channel-types, commit 6d1f578a7af725ed16044152e5bb3ab956089bd9
    (adds `filters.for-channel-types` / `jobs.for-channel-types`, required
    for the BS4K remux).  Statically linked against musl (MIT,
    LICENSES/MIT-musl.txt) and the Rust crates listed in the fork's
    Cargo.lock, each under its own license.

  * mirakc-arib 0.24.20
    https://github.com/mirakc/mirakc-arib -- GPL-2.0-or-later
    (LICENSES/GPL-2.0.txt)
    Unmodified binary taken from the official mirakc/tools:alpine
    linux/arm/v7 image.  The corresponding source is the upstream tag 0.24.20
    (commit 28b1bfc2e6f929b721d4c876709860811da1df35), which also pins the
    statically linked dependencies (LibISDB, aribb24, ...).
    https://github.com/mirakc/mirakc-arib/tree/0.24.20

  * dantto4k
    https://github.com/nekohkr/dantto4k -- Apache-2.0 (LICENSE)
    Built from commit 7d9c7e25e0c398a072b5e328c58f58b062f8a979 with the
    armv7 portability patch in tools/dantto4k/ (build steps are there too).
    Statically linked against:
      - TSDuck (submodule fbbed98, BSD-2-Clause, LICENSES/BSD-2-Clause-TSDuck.txt)
      - asio (submodule 03ae834, BSL-1.0, LICENSES/BSL-1.0-asio.txt)
      - zlib 1.3.2 (Zlib, LICENSES/Zlib.txt)
      - musl (MIT, LICENSES/MIT-musl.txt)
      - libstdc++ / libgcc (GPL-3.0 with the GCC Runtime Library Exception)
    The ACAS/AES-NI path is stubbed out in this build; it must be run with
    --frontend-descrambled.

  * tuner-stream-*, b21dec, b61dec
    Built from src/ in this repository (Apache-2.0, from
    pix-smb400-mirakurun).  Dynamically linked against the device's own
    Android system libraries, which are not redistributed here.
    The usage text of b61dec (src/b61dec.c and bin/b61dec) is modified from
    the original: a hard-coded key string was replaced with a placeholder of
    the same length.  The key is supplied at run time with -key.
